After the first CI run, GitHub's repository Actions setting changed from
allowed_actions=all to allowed_actions=local_only. The ci workflow uses
actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-python@v5, and
dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable, which local_only does not permit.
This is the leading explanation for startup_failure; a fresh run after the
setting change will test it.

The operator said the local-only choice was a misunderstanding and authorized
correcting it. GitHub readback after the correction:
enabled=true
allowed_actions=selected
github_owned_allowed=false
verified_allowed=false
patterns_allowed=[actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-python@v5,
                  dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable]
fork PR approval=all_external_contributors
main enforce_admins=true, allow_force_pushes=false, allow_deletions=false

